+
+Reviewed `kg/merge-trainer-lanes` at `f4ecd90ec15cf09adcd20570aedf636324ffac30`
+against integration `f464c3db45449ce362fde25c5d9b37f88ad20e5e` and approved
+lanes `4cac1a1`, `530b8cc`, `71cebdb`, and `bb0f7e4`. All are ancestors of
+HEAD. This is a read-only staging merge review, not native trainer or GPU
+qualification.
+
+No actionable findings. The prior report at
+`/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-merge-trainer-lanes-r1.md`
+contains one P3: the grammar-heads Reference called the startup assertion open.
+HEAD fixes it at
+`cookbook/references/kaggriculture-grammar-heads-sit-behind-isaiahs-actor-projection.md:73`,
+links the completed configs implementation, and retains the trainer integration
+gap. All findings in that report are resolved.
+
+## Requested checks
+
+| Check | Result | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| `uv run pytest tests/kaggriculture tests/owl tests/scripts tests/tools -m 'not slow' -q` | 1,458 passed, 5 skipped; exit 0; 33.20 s | `pytest.log` |
+| `uv run mypy python/owl scripts` | 60 source files clean; exit 0 | `mypy.log` |
+| Same pytest selection, collection only | 1,463 cases | `collection.log` |
+
+Collection: Kaggriculture 352; owl 795; scripts 210; tools 106. Combining the
+collection with the run's explicit skips gives Kaggriculture 351 passed / 1
+skipped and the retained owl/scripts/tools suites 1,107 passed / 4 skipped.
+The latter includes new Kaggriculture seam tests in the shared scripts suite.
+
+The five skips are the native grammar binding, two FlashAttention/CUDA cases,
+the unavailable x86 quantized backend, and native Kaggriculture evaluation.
+None is waiting on model or config registration.
+
+## Preservation and merge semantics
+
+- HEAD has 830 Python test definitions. No integration test name is missing.
+  The parent union is preserved after normalizing two trim-test renames that
+  already occurred in integration. The replacements retain the old assertions
+  and extend them to `grammar_kernel.rs` and the three-file authored inventory.
+  See `test-preservation/summary.json` and that directory's detailed evidence.
+- Rust source, including engine code and tests, is byte-identical to integration.
+  Briefs 1.4/1.5 are byte-identical to their approved `bb0f7e4` parent.
+- Across changed production Python files, no parent function is missing.
+  Only `FullConfig._validate_cross_config_constraints` and `_create_eval_env`
+  have function bodies differing from every approved parent; both are reviewed
+  merge resolutions. Other production functions match a parent by AST.
+- `python/owl/train/config.py:118` runs `_validate_kaggriculture_rl` followed
+  by `_validate_kaggriculture_training`. Typed env/model pairing rejects mixed
+  games; Orbit retains its original helper constraints. An independent
+  differential probe compared integration's validator with HEAD on 28 Orbit
+  configs times 128 setting combinations: 3,584 probes, 728 accepted by both,
+  zero accept/reject differences.
+- `scripts/run_ppo.py:155` loads `FullConfig` through its real loader.
+  Lines 162–168 finalize per-rank runtime shapes and check the registered
+  `cfg.model`. The check precedes run directory, env and model allocation.
+  Fresh launch, override rejection and resume tests retain the real loader
+  and pass in the requested suite.
+- `_create_eval_env` still rejects Kaggriculture before native env construction,
+  then narrows Orbit with `require_orbit_env` and preserves its constructor
+  arguments. Raw-bank scoring, seed constraints, promotion telemetry and
+  truncation semantics match their approved parent.
+- Registration-dependent tests now load the actual shipped configurations and
+  build the model or validate the intended guard failures. The activated YAML
+  guard test checks all three configs against gamma, value-loss, reward-mode
+  and clipping overrides. These tests execute successfully; native-dependent
+  placeholders remain skipped.
+
+## Documentation and scope
+
+All parent cookbook log entries and index link targets survive. The current
+merge count statement matches its committed prepare receipt: engine 87, root
+Rust 164 passed / 2 ignored, Python 1,458 passed / 5 skipped. These Rust counts
+were checked against the receipt, not rerun in this review. Historical lane
+counts remain attributed to those lanes. See `docs/preservation.json`.
